<!--
  RM_Miasma_Predators.xml                            MIASMA_FLORA_ROSTER_1

  The five predatory plants of miasma_flora_roster_2026-09-23.md §5 — a
  separate clade from the rainbow blooms, NOT bound by ban 2, honestly and
  visibly predatory. Owner ruling: they take the arthropod-floor scuttlers,
  never a colonist and never a tame animal.

  MIASMA_SCUTTLER_PREDATION_1 (this pass): real carnivory C# now wired via
  RM_CompPlantPredator/RM_CompProperties_PlantPredator
  (src/RimMandrake/Miasma/Source/), self-contained in this assembly — no
  compile-time reference to RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors needed, since prey
  is matched by a plain defName whitelist (RM_Karravel/RM_Karrobel/
  RM_Karrimeth/RM_Karrolun), same idiom RM_CompVerminBreeder's
  breedFoodThingDefNames already uses. Desktop check (RimSage against
  decompiled 1.6 source) confirmed the engine question this file used to
  flag as UNMEASURABLE: Plant never overrides Tick(), only TickLong(), and
  ThingWithComps.TickLong() does call CompTickLong() on every comp — so a
  plant CAN carry a ticking predator comp with no manual interval throttle
  needed. Restricted to wild (unfactioned) pawns of exactly the four named
  defNames — never a colonist or tame animal, per the ruling below. Tell:
  a floating mote at the kill site ("<plant> feeds"), real for all five now;
  each plant's own unique visual tell (cloudy vessel, closed blades,
  scuttler-free mud) stays a future ART/graphic-state pass, not built here.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="PlantBase">
    <defName>RM_Ullavess</defName>
    <label>ullavess</label>
    <description>A group of tall tapering vessels standing mouth-up, each half-full of clear fluid you can see into. The outer wall is veined maroon over yellow-green; the rim is a hard iridescent lip and the inside wall is glassy and visibly slick. Spent vessels below are brown and collapsed. Ullavess is the clade's anchor — the plant a player recognises as a predator on sight — and a cloudy vessel means it has fed recently.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Plant/RM_Ullavess/RM_Ullavess_a</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>1.1</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>50</MaxHitPoints>
      <Nutrition>0.1</Nutrition>
      <Flammability>0.4</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <plant>
      <fertilityMin>0.1</fertilityMin>
      <fertilitySensitivity>0.15</fertilitySensitivity>
      <growDays>9</growDays>
      <visualSizeRange>0.8~1.3</visualSizeRange>
      <topWindExposure>0.1</topWindExposure>
      <wildOrder>1</wildOrder>
      <wildClusterRadius>5</wildClusterRadius>
      <wildClusterWeight>25</wildClusterWeight>
    </plant>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.Miasma.RM_CompProperties_PlantPredator">
        <preyDefNames>
          <li>RM_Karravel</li>
          <li>RM_Karrobel</li>
          <li>RM_Karrimeth</li>
          <li>RM_Karrolun</li>
        </preyDefNames>
        <huntRadius>2</huntRadius>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="PlantBase">
    <defName>RM_Nemreth</defName>
    <label>nemreth</label>
    <description>A low mat of hair-fine red stalks, each ending in a clear glistening bead that holds the light like dew and never dries. From a distance the whole mat glitters; close up, the beads are thick and drawn into threads, and older stalks are curled inward around what they caught. The most beautiful thing in the biome that is also a killer, and it never pretended otherwise — its adhesive is the luxury attar's binder.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Plant/RM_Nemreth/RM_Nemreth_a</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>0.75</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>30</MaxHitPoints>
      <Nutrition>0.04</Nutrition>
      <Flammability>0.3</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <plant>
      <fertilityMin>0.05</fertilityMin>
      <fertilitySensitivity>0.1</fertilitySensitivity>
      <growDays>5</growDays>
      <visualSizeRange>0.4~0.7</visualSizeRange>
      <topWindExposure>0</topWindExposure>
      <wildOrder>1</wildOrder>
      <wildClusterRadius>6</wildClusterRadius>
      <wildClusterWeight>15</wildClusterWeight>
    </plant>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.Miasma.RM_CompProperties_PlantPredator">
        <preyDefNames>
          <li>RM_Karravel</li>
