  <ThingDef ParentName="PlantBase">
    <defName>RM_Braskeen</defName>
    <label>braskeen</label>
    <description>A flat whorl lying on the surface, each arm ending in a pair of hinged blades held slightly open, fringed with stiff interlocking teeth. The blades close when something touches them and stay shut for a day with the catch showing between the teeth. Blade interiors are a raw wet pink. The only plant on the page with real motion — a channel of these snapping shut one after another as scuttlers cross is the biome's best ambient moment.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <!-- Graphic_Random over RM_BraskeenA (open) / RM_BraskeenB (closed) —
           ambient variety of both states scattered across a bed. The actual
           touch-triggered snap animation needs the same future predation
